  "cause_explanation": "The original answer failed to establish a direct, named-company exposure for 'EV battery trays aluminum enclosures' under Section 232. While the source text contains an official Federal Register scope definition explicitly listing 'electric vehicle battery trays' as subject merchandise under Aluminum Extrusions AD/CVD orders (not Section 232), and mentions Section 232 steel/aluminum tariffs affecting EV costs, no passage links a specific company to these duties or confirms the current applicability of Section 232 specifically to aluminum enclosures for this product type. The evidence is fragmented between general industry impact reports and a","confidence": "high",
  "remaining_gap": "The original answer did not distinguish between Section 232 (steel/aluminum) and AD/CVD (aluminum extrusions) regimes, nor did it identify the specific product scope inclusion for battery trays in the Federal Register text. The lack of a named company or facility in the evidence prevents establishing 'company applicability' as required.","recovery_assessment": "partial_cached_support",
